# Roadmap

Wyrd is pre-release. The docs cover what runs today; this page covers what is
**specified or in progress but not yet wired** for users. It exists so the shape
of the system is visible without the rest of the docs implying more than ships.

<Aside title="Reading this page" data-variant="wyrd">

"Specified" means schemas, types, and validation exist. "In progress" means there
is working code behind an internal or preview boundary. Neither is a supported,
documented surface yet.

</Aside>

## Cards beyond Data, Model, and Prompt

Thirteen card kinds plus `External` are **specified** — their schemas and
validation structs exist and appear in the [schema reference](/api/schemas/) — but
none has a card holder, Python surface, or runnable example yet. The
[Cards overview](/cards/) marks each one. Bringing a kind to "shipped" means a
holder, a Python/Rust authoring path, registration, and an example.

`Agent` and `Workflow` are a special case: the cards are spec-only, but the
runnable thing already exists as the [Skald runtime](/skald/). The cards are the
declarative records; the runtime is the execution.

## Drift monitoring

A drift engine (PSI and SPC computations) exists and is tested in `vala-drift`, but
nothing consumes it yet — no server endpoint, CLI command, or Python entry point.
Drift is real code without a user-facing surface. When it lands, a `Drift` card
will declare the monitor and the registry will run it.

## Server surfaces still to come

- **Dedicated card reads over REST** — upload and download work today; a
  first-class `GET` for an individual card by identity is not yet exposed.
- **gRPC card services** — the gRPC server currently serves health only. Card
  operations over gRPC are not implemented.

## Delegation (preview)

Token-exchange and act-as delegation (`/auth/token` `TokenExchange`) exist behind a
preview gate and are **off in production**. Until that gate opens, the supported
auth surfaces are API keys, Wyrd-JWTs, and OIDC federation — see
[Authentication](/server/auth/).

## Bifrost — analytical storage

Bifrost is Wyrd's OLAP path over Apache Iceberg and DataFusion. It is **internal
and ongoing**: no Python consumer, no documented API, no user-facing surface yet.
It will back analytical queries over observations and evaluation records once it
lands. For now it is engine work, not a feature.

## What this page replaces

Earlier drafts of these docs carried design essays, threat models, and tech specs
for systems that aren't built. Those live in the repository where engineers read
them. This page is the public-facing remainder: the vision, stated as roadmap, not
as how-to.
